// №948 boundary pin B5 (audit PoC p07) — FLIPPED by №951.
// The each-accumulator loss: the loop body raised the label of `acc`, and
// the sink-gate walker DISCARDED the body environment at loop exit, while
// the neighbouring `while` arm folded it back. That asymmetry was the gap.
// Now the fold is the same for both loop forms and this program is the
// [PII_EGRESS_OUTPUT] refusal — a leak-suite negative.
pattern P(x: String) -> String { let mut acc = "" each c in split(env("SP"), "") { acc = acc + c } print(acc) return "ok" }
flow Main { input: String = "x" -> P -> output }
